API.md E3, E1: over examples/features/entries, AddEntry of a key an entry file already holds
(blade) is ErrKeyExists, so the duplicate key a check reports as E3101 is never written; the
refusal names the second op, after a first one that applied.
-- options --
example: features/entries
pkgs: features.entries
-- edit.json --
{"ops": [
  {"op": "addEntry", "path": "items", "key": "mace", "source": "{ name: \"Mace\", kind: sword }"},
  {"op": "addEntry", "path": "items", "key": "blade", "source": "{ name: \"Another\", kind: sword }"}
]}
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- result.json --
{
  "error": "op 1: key already exists"
}
